{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Kirana 0.4 has been on npm since 6 November, and 0.4.2 is its newest release.\nEvery package is released at the same version, so update all the Kirana packages\nyour project lists together, then run:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"$ npx kirana-style@latest doctor","lang":"console","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> kirana-style@latest doctor","variant":"terminal"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"doctor","source":"doctor"}},{"type":"text","value":" reads your project and says when its Kirana packages are not all on one\nrelease. This post covers the whole 0.4 line: the two changes that can alter\nwhat a build gives you, what is new, and how the three releases went."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"breaking-production-builds-write-dense-class-names","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Breaking: production builds write dense class names"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A class name carries two hashes, one for its condition and one for its value.\nA production build now replaces both with codes of one or two characters,\nnumbered across the whole application, so "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"k50-<span class=\"th-token th-type\">KFHz_D9ur</span>","source":"k50-KFHz_D9ur"}},{"type":"text","value":" ships as something like\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"k50-b_a","source":"k50-b_a"}},{"type":"text","value":". Variable tokens and keyframes that only the stylesheet names get\nshort names the same way."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Merging works exactly as before, and nothing extra ships to the browser. What it\nsaves depends on the application. The latest run of\n"},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/building/output#dense-names","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the benchmarks"}]},{"type":"text","value":", against hashed names: the\nCSS in gzip, not measured; what a page downloads,\nnot measured."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What can notice the change:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anything that reads class names from a production build,"}]},{"type":"text","value":" such as an\nend-to-end test or a snapshot. The development server, the language server\nand "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">kirana-style</span> trace","source":"kirana-style trace"}},{"type":"text","value":" keep the hashed names."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Caching between deploys."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The shortest codes go to the most used values, so\na change elsewhere in the application can renumber them, and a chunk whose\nsource did not change may still be downloaded again."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Either way, "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-property\">names</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;hashed&quot;</span>","source":"names: \"hashed\""}},{"type":"text","value":" in the plugin's options keeps the old names. A\nproject with a "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/frameworks/server-templates","children":[{"type":"text","value":"class map"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for server\ntemplates keeps them on its own. The\n"},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/integrations/vite#dense-names","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vite guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" has the details."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"breaking-a-given-classname-wins-over-an-element-s-own-sx","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Breaking: a given className wins over an element's own sx"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When an element has both its own "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"sx","source":"sx"}},{"type":"text","value":" and a "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"className","source":"className"}},{"type":"text","value":" handed to it, the two\nwere always merged. The given class now merges last, as a caller's "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"sx","source":"sx"}},{"type":"text","value":" would,\nso where both set the same property, the given class wins:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"<div {...props} sx={styles.root} />\n// props.className, from a render prop or a parent, wins over styles.root","lang":"tsx","html":"&lt;<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">div</span> {...props} <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">sx</span>={styles.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">root</span>} /&gt;\n<span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// props.className, from a render prop or a parent, wins over styles.root</span>"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is what a headless library's render prop expects: the outer part's classes\nwin over the rendered component's own, as they do in shadcn/ui. If one of your\ncomponents relied on its own "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"sx","source":"sx"}},{"type":"text","value":" winning, put that style last in an "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"sx","source":"sx"}},{"type":"text","value":" array\ninstead. "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/styling/sx","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The sx prop"}]},{"type":"text","value":" has the rule."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"moving-an-existing-project-over","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Moving an existing project over"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Two codemods rewrite an existing codebase into Kirana styles, one for\nstyled-components (and Emotion) and one for CSS Modules. Each prints its diff and\na report first, and applies it with "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-attr\">--write</span>","source":"--write"}},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"$ npx kirana-style migrate styled-components src\n$ npx kirana-style migrate css-modules src --write","lang":"console","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> kirana-style migrate styled-components src\n<span class=\"th-token th-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> kirana-style migrate css-modules src <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">--write</span>","variant":"terminal"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The report names what a codemod cannot decide for you, such as CSS whose result\ndepended on which file loaded first. The guides walk through\nwhat changes, from\n"},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/migration/from-styled-components","children":[{"type":"text","value":"styled-components"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and from\n"},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/migration/from-css-modules","children":[{"type":"text","value":"CSS Modules"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"components-on-more-frameworks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Components on more frameworks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">kirana-style</span> ui","source":"kirana-style ui"}},{"type":"text","value":", the command that installs components from a registry into your\nproject, now installs on Svelte, Solid and Angular. Along the 0.4 line it also\nlearned to:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"start a new app from a registry's template:"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> @kirana-style/registry init <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">--template</span> vite-react my-app","source":"npx @kirana-style/registry init --template vite-react my-app"}},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"work in a monorepo,"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with the components in a package every app imports, as\nshadcn/ui's monorepo template has them;"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"build a registry from your own sources"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"ui build","source":"ui build"}},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"serve your registries to an AI assistant"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"ui mcp","source":"ui mcp"}},{"type":"text","value":", so it can search\nthem, read an item and get the command that installs it\n("},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/tooling/mcp","children":[{"type":"text","value":"registries for AI assistants"}]},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"/docs/tooling/components","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installing components"}]},{"type":"text","value":" covers all of it."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"typed-states-for-more-libraries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Typed states for more libraries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"@kirana-style/states","source":"@kirana-style/states"}},{"type":"text","value":" turns a headless library's data attributes into typed\ncondition keys. 0.4 adds vocabularies for ui-sdk and for Kirana UI Primitives,\nand follows each of their releases, so a part's states are a type check away\ninstead of a string you type by hand. The\n"},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/styling/states","children":[{"type":"text","value":"component states"}]},{"type":"text","value":" guide lists every library."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"smaller-things-worth-knowing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Smaller things worth knowing"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solid 2"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is supported: "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"sx","source":"sx"}},{"type":"text","value":" is typed on "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"@solidjs/web","source":"@solidjs/web"}},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"init","source":"init"}},{"type":"text","value":" detects it,\nand there is a template for it ("},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/frameworks/solid#solid-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solid guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Desktop and mobile apps"}]},{"type":"text","value":" have guides, on Electron, Tauri, Electrobun and\nCapacitor ("},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/frameworks/desktop","children":[{"type":"text","value":"desktop and mobile"}]},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A hover on a large style"}]},{"type":"text","value":" shows its first rules and conditional values and\ncounts the rest, so the card stays readable."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Faster builds and edits."}]},{"type":"text","value":" A build hands the engine many modules in one\ncall, a large module's compile time grows in step with its styles, an\nunchanged module is answered before it is read again, and styles\nthat read tokens compile once per session."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"how-0-4-came-together","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How 0.4 came together"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"0.4.0, 6 November:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" dense names, the className rule, both codemods, and\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">kirana-style</span> ui","source":"kirana-style ui"}},{"type":"text","value":" on Svelte, Solid and Angular with "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"ui build","source":"ui build"}},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"ui mcp","source":"ui mcp"}},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"0.4.1, 9 November:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" apps from a registry's template, components in a\nmonorepo, and "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"ui init","source":"ui init"}},{"type":"text","value":" setting up React Router, Nuxt and SvelteKit."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"0.4.2, 20 November:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Solid 2, the ui-sdk and Kirana UI Primitives\nvocabularies, and fixes for what the first projects on 0.4 ran into."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every change, with its pull request, is in "},{"type":"link","href":"/changelog","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the changelog"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"breaking-production-builds-write-dense-class-names","text":"Breaking: production builds write dense class names","level":2},{"id":"breaking-a-given-classname-wins-over-an-element-s-own-sx","text":"Breaking: a given className wins over an element's own sx","level":2},{"id":"moving-an-existing-project-over","text":"Moving an existing project over","level":2},{"id":"components-on-more-frameworks","text":"Components on more frameworks","level":2},{"id":"typed-states-for-more-libraries","text":"Typed states for more libraries","level":2},{"id":"smaller-things-worth-knowing","text":"Smaller things worth knowing","level":2},{"id":"how-0-4-came-together","text":"How 0.4 came together","level":2}]}
